7. Climate: Thank You for Accepting Delivery

The environmental component is perhaps the most darkly comic because the age distribution is impossible to miss.

An eighteen-year-old in 2026 was born in approximately 2008.

A twenty-four-year-old was born in approximately 2002.

The IPCC estimates that cumulative net human CO₂ emissions between 1850 and 2019 reached approximately 2,400 ± 240 gigatonnes.

Fifty-eight percent occurred before 1990. (IPCC)

The people currently aged 18–24 were therefore children for effectively the entire historical emissions period measured there.

By 2019 they were approximately eleven to seventeen years old.

Not generally the chairmen of oil companies.

Not usually transport ministers.

Rarely responsible for national energy policy.

Nevertheless, delivery has now been completed.

ITEM: Planetary climate system
CONDITION: Used
PREVIOUS OWNERS: Numerous
RETURN WINDOW: Closed
REPAIR RESPONSIBILITY: Yours
PLEASE RATE YOUR EXPERIENCE: ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

The World Meteorological Organization reported in March 2026 that 2015–2025 were the eleven hottest years on record, with 2025 roughly 1.43°C above the 1850–1900 average. (World Meteorological Organization)

The appropriate generational response is apparently optimism.

Young people are expected to acknowledge the problem, finance adaptation, change consumption patterns, accept changing employment, tolerate energy transitions, inherit infrastructure built for another climate and then avoid being overly dramatic about any of it.

This is rather like setting fire to somebody’s kitchen, handing them the extinguisher and criticising their negative attitude toward interior design.

