8. The Fundamental Attribution Error, But Make It National Policy

The recurring mechanism throughout these examples is remarkably consistent.

Structural deterioration is converted into personal pathology.

Expensive housing becomes insufficient saving.

Precarious employment becomes insufficient work ethic.

Fear of automation becomes resistance to progress.

Psychological distress becomes victimhood.

Climate anxiety becomes catastrophising.

The institution remains innocent because the individual remains defective.

This produces what might be called the National Fundamental Attribution Machine:

[
\boxed{
\text{Bad Outcome}
\rightarrow
\text{Individual Behaviour}
}
]

rather than:

[
\boxed{
\text{Bad Outcome}
\rightarrow
\text{Investigate Individual + System}
}
]

The second expression requires work.

The first fits comfortably onto breakfast television.

